# Additional permission under GNU AGPL version 3 section 7

Copyright (C) 2026 Odin Loch

## Why this exists

MathScript is licensed under AGPL-3.0-or-later. When built with `MS_ENABLE_CUDA=ON`
it links against the NVIDIA CUDA runtime and the cuBLAS, cuSOLVER and NCCL
libraries, which are distributed under NVIDIA's proprietary end-user licence and
are not compatible with the AGPL.

The "System Libraries" exclusion in GPLv3 section 1 is arguable for the CUDA
driver, which ships with the operating system's hardware support, and weak for
cuBLAS, cuSOLVER and NCCL, which do not. Without an explicit grant, distributing
a CUDA-enabled binary would infringe this project's own licence. As sole
copyright holder, Odin Loch grants that permission here.

## The grant

As an additional permission under section 7 of the GNU Affero General Public
License version 3, you have permission to link or combine any covered work with
the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit libraries -- including but not limited to the CUDA
runtime, cuBLAS, cuSOLVER, cuFFT, cuRAND, cuSPARSE and NCCL -- and to convey the
resulting work. The terms of the AGPL continue to apply to the covered work
itself.

If you modify this work, you may extend this permission to your version, but you
are not obliged to. If you do not wish to extend it, delete this statement from
your version.

## What this permission does not do

- It does not relicense the covered work. Everything outside the NVIDIA
  libraries remains under AGPL-3.0-or-later, including the AGPL section 13
  obligation to offer source to users interacting with the work over a network.
- It does not grant any right in NVIDIA's software. Their EULA governs your use
  of the CUDA libraries independently of this permission.
- It does not extend to any other proprietary library. A combination with
  something other than the NVIDIA CUDA libraries is not covered here.

## Scope

The permission applies to the whole covered work when built with CUDA support.
Files that participate directly in that link -- `src/cuda/` and its headers under
`include/ms/cuda/` -- name this file in their SPDX `LicenseRef` header so the
grant is discoverable from the source rather than only from the repository root.
